  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full set at The Black Sheep in Colorado Springs on August 18, 2021, captured in a recording that includes twenty-three songs over 107 minutes [1]. This performance is the 308th in the archive’s collection for the band, following a show at Saturn on August 8, 2021 [3]. The setlist opens with a cover of Rickie Lee Jones’ “We Belong Together,” which is the only archived performance of that song [1][3]. The band then plays a mix of tracks from albums like *Getting Into Knives* and *Transcendental Youth*, including “Aulon Raid,” “Cry for Judas,” and “Dark in Here” [1]. Notable rarities include “Rat Queen,” which has only two archived performances, and “Rescue Breathing,” with just three [3]. The set features several bustouts, such as “Rotten Stinking Mouthpiece,” the first in 88 shows, and “Nine Black Poppies,” the first in 59 shows [3]. The performance concludes with five encore songs, including “Up The Wolves” and “This Year” [1]. The recommended recording is a matrix mix of soundboard and audience microphones, taped and transferred by the uploader, who thanks the venue and the band for supporting live concert archival [1]. The thumbnail for the upload was created by the uploader’s fiancé [1].",
